.TH NVDA-RDP-SETTINGS 1 2026-11-25 "nvda-rdp-linux 0.5.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
nvda-rdp-settings \- read and change the driver settings of NVDA on the RDP client
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B nvda-rdp-settings
.BR speech | braille
.B list
.br
.B nvda-rdp-settings
.BR speech | braille
.B get
.I id
.br
.B nvda-rdp-settings
.BR speech | braille
.B values
.I id
.br
.B nvda-rdp-settings
.BR speech | braille
.B set
.I id value
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B nvda-rdp-settings
runs in a session served by
.BR nvda-rdp-server (7)
and reaches the NVDA screen reader of the RDP client through RDAccess: the
settings of its synthesizer
.RB ( speech )
or of its braille display driver
.RB ( braille ).
.PP
NVDA reports its settings only if
.I driver settings management
is allowed in RDAccess's settings on the client; it is off by default.
Without it,
.B list
says that NVDA reports no settings.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B list
Each setting, one per line: its id, its value, its name in NVDA and, for
a number, its range.
.TP
.BI get " id"
One setting.
.TP
.BI values " id"
The possible values of a setting that is neither a number nor on/off,
such as
.BR voice :
their id, name and, for a voice, language.
.TP
.BI set " id value"
Change a setting. The value is a whole number within the range, one of
.BR on ,
.BR off ,
.BR true ,
.BR false ,
.BR yes ,
.BR no ,
or the id or the name (case ignored) of a possible value.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success; 1 if the server of the channel does not answer, NVDA is not
attached to the channel, or the setting or value is not valid.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
nvda-rdp-settings speech list
nvda-rdp-settings speech values voice
nvda-rdp-settings speech set voice "Microsoft Zira \- English (United States)"
nvda-rdp-settings speech set rate 60
nvda-rdp-settings braille list
.fi
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/nvda-rdp-server/speech-settings.sock
.TQ
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/nvda-rdp-server/braille-settings.sock
Sockets of the speech module and of the braille server, readable by the
user only.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR nvda-rdp-server (7),
.BR orca (1)
